<title>BELGIUM: Belgian regulator withdraws Fischer bank licence.</title>
<headline>Belgian regulator withdraws Fischer bank licence.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's regulatory Banking and Finance Commission (BFC) said on Thursday it had revoked the banking licence of Antwerp bank Max Fischer with immediate effect.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission has established that as a result of serious irregularities, the good outcome of the commitments of Bank Max Fischer is threatened,&quot; the BFC said in a statement.</p>
<p>No one was available at the bank for comment.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
